00:02:12.844 --> 00:02:15.275
Your turn. Say: fresh produce.

43
00:02:17.975 --> 00:02:19.011
fresh produce.

44
00:02:20.017 --> 00:02:22.156
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:22.456 --> 00:02:24.908
I've been feeling tired and stressed lately.

46
00:02:26.217 --> 00:02:29.287
You should take care of your mental health. Are you sleeping enough?

47
00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:33.270
Not really. I'm on my phone until midnight.

48
00:02:34.583 --> 00:02:37.874
You'd better stop that. Screen fatigue can affect your sleep.

49
00:02:39.183 --> 00:02:40.382
What else should I do?

50
00:02:41.683 --> 00:02:46.458
You ought to start a healthy routine: a short workout, fresh produce and lots of water.

51
00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:50.168
Grammar focus: should · ought to · had better.

52
00:02:50.468 --> 00:02:52.409
Use should or ought to for advice.

53
00:02:52.709 --> 00:02:55.661
Use had better for strong advice or a warning.

54
00:02:55.961 --> 00:03:00.192
For example: You should drink more water. You'd better stop, or you'll get ill.

55
00:03:00.492 --> 00:03:05.533
Had better is stronger than should and often suggests a bad result if you don't follow the advice.

56
00:03:06.517 --> 00:03:09.552
Now read and listen. Small Habits, Big Changes.

57
00:03:09.852 --> 00:03:13.175
Doctors say that small daily habits can improve our wellbeing.

58
00:03:14.483 --> 00:03:17.667
A ten-minute workout is better than no exercise at all.

59
00:03:18.983 --> 00:03:21.993
Staying hydrated helps us concentrate and reduces headaches.

60
00:03:23.283 --> 00:03:27.558
Turning off screens an hour before bed can reduce anxiety and improve sleep.

61
00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:32.080
Experts say we should eat fresh produce with every meal.

62
00:03:33.383 --> 00:03:35.862
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:36.162 --> 00:03:38.742
A feeling of worry or nervousness is blank.

64
00:03:39.042 --> 00:03:42.289
A, wellbeing. B, anxiety. C, workout.

65
00:03:46.283 --> 00:03:48.225
The answer is B: anxiety.

66
00:03:49.717 --> 00:03:52.056
You look ill. You blank see a doctor.

67
00:03:52.356 --> 00:03:55.115
A, should. B, shouldn't. C, had.

68
00:03:59.117 --> 00:04:01.116
The answer is A: should.

69
00:04:02.617 --> 00:04:04.872
You blank leave now, or you'll miss the bus.

70
00:04:05.172 --> 00:04:08.047
A, had better. B, ought. C, should to.

71
00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:13.574
The answer is A: had better.

72
00:04:15.083 --> 00:04:17.362
Tiredness from looking at screens is blank.

73
00:04:17.662 --> 00:04:21.919
A, screen fatigue. B, mental health. C, fresh produce.

74
00:04:25.917 --> 00:04:28.102
The answer is A: screen fatigue.

75
00:04:29.617 --> 00:04:33.114
According to the text, turning off screens before bed can blank.

76
00:04:33.414 --> 00:04:38.135
A, cause headaches. B, reduce anxiety. C, replace exercise.

77
00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:44.579
The answer is B: reduce anxiety.

78
00:04:46.083 --> 00:04:49.653
Now it's your turn to speak. What advice would you give to a stressed friend?

79
00:04:54.953 --> 00:04:59.356
You should take short breaks, go for a walk and talk to someone you trust.

80
00:04:59.656 --> 00:05:00.982
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:01.983 --> 00:05:05.541
Great work today! You learned eight new words and should · ought to · had better.

82
00:05:05.841 --> 00:05:09.144
Today's value is healthy body. Move your body every day.

83
00:05:09.444 --> 00:05:12.061
